 A trivial example:
 
 ```python
@@ -131,3 +135,11 @@ html1 = md.convert(text_with_footnote)
 md.reset()
 html2 = md.convert(text_without_footnote)
 ```
+
+## Footnote Order
+
+By default, footnotes are numbered and listed in the order in which they are
+first referenced in the document, regardless of the order in which they are
+defined. Footnotes which are defined but never referenced are listed after
+all referenced footnotes, in definition order. Set `USE_DEFINITION_ORDER` to
+`True` to number and list footnotes in the order they are defined instead.
